{"title":"2016 UMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Four fair six-sided dice are rolled. What is the probability that they can be divided into two pairs which sum to the same value? For example, a roll of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99bdaf5eb31c59d6576495951d3f3eeae3fc5868.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,4,6,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> can be divided into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/1/621f951230bd018717e8c0c5cd3bfd6b1f8720a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/563948106c3332662355412547d99acab218c16f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />, each of which sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, but a roll of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/a/b5a83c75f792d07516f241a4c246abca1f6a6714.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1,5,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> cannot be divided into two pairs that sum to the same value.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We split this into cases based on the the form of the unordered values shown on the dice. In the following, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/2/2b2b9cec140507454d58c3cc7f3a8f4c2784d414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt;= a,b,c,d &lt;= 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"153\" height=\"16\" /> are distinct numbers. After determining the (unordered) numbers that can appear on the dice, we must determine how many ways we can order those dice rolls in sequence. \n</p><p>Case1: The unordered numbers shown are {a,a,a,a} In this case, it is clear that the pairing (a,a) and (a,a) will yield equal sums, so we have 6 possible choices for a, and this is the number of possible rolls that take this form. \n</p><p>Case2: The unordered numbers shown are {a,a,a,b} In this case, one of the pairs will contain b, hence the pairs will be (a,b) and (a,a). But these can never be equal as a 6= b. \n</p><p>Case3: The unordered numbers shown are {a,a,b,b} To obtain equal sums, we must split the numbers into the pairs (a,b) and (a,b). There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/b/6cb253d1a78a22ad076662873c97522db3634fe2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{6}{2}= 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" /> ways to select a and b, and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/28489cc9af0f13d0dcf5298be73a3fd2289152ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{4}{2}= 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> ways to order the rolls (select two of the rolls to be a’s). Hence there are 15·6 = 90 total rolls that take this form. \n</p><p>Case4: The unordered numbers shown are {a,a,b,c} In this case, either b pairs with a or b pairs with c. If b pairs with a, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3dadd085d9bb36437c83606adeb69e7d0439b466.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b = c + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" /> , which is impossible as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18cb78e5ac5ae10adb75e6af496ee5b30347454c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\ne c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore, b must pair with c, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c92c20d6f536c94ad7ba9636dcf7525c140d2589.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a = b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, b + c is even. We may assume without loss of generality that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/2/f42e638023bd7080e4b131fedd5a6d1db0911d71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt;= c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"54\" height=\"13\" />, hence the possibilities for (b,c) are (b,c) = (1,3),(1,5),(2,4),(2,6),(3,5),(4,6).\nTherefore, there are six ways to choose (b,c), and a is automatically determined (it is the average of b and c). Then there are 4! 2! = 12 ways to order the rolls, hence there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d28a22db60cf2d01a2c40f35d33d55cfcf33e23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\cdot 12 = 72$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" /> total rolls that take this form. \n</p><p>Case5: The unordered numbers shown are {a,b,c,d} In this case, the sum of the pairs must be representable in at two ways with distinct integers. We ﬁnd\n5 = 1 + 4 = 2 + 3;  6 = 1 + 5 = 2 + 4; 7 = 1 + 6 = 2 + 5 = 3 + 4; 8 = 2 + 6 = 3 + 5; 9 = 3 + 6 = 4 + 5.\nThese are the only numbers that can be represented as the sum of two numbers in at least two ways using distinct numbers. In particular, for the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3bba0581f09c6d2342c7b7ad47844cc934dbed2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,6,8,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />,we know immediately what the four numbers a,b,c,d are. For 7,we must choose two of the three pairs, and we can do this in three ways. Therefore, the number of ways to choose {a,b,c,d} is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/8/c388c6cbbfa2fb1bd0368708b90e23040c21684a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+1+1+1+3 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"167\" height=\"14\" />. Then we can order the rolls in 4! = 24 ways. Thus there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/1/9d1409515321f1e85c928dbb3cf9ce9bdeca15a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\cdot 24 = 168$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> total rolls that take this form. Adding these together, we ﬁnd <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/5/c4511b129e60e476edabd2dd810017db58fbc215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 90 + 72 + 168 = 336$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"190\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/1711e36a4e651d2f2407a19560fc2c39f005d00d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{336}{64} = \\frac{7}{27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"76\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We observe\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/c/2acb3b3fed040cb65fafec73bd1365ff97f5d4fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{Probability}=\\frac{\\textbf{Favorable}}{\\textbf{Total}}.\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/0364809949010d0cb397d5da8c5754ad079178ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Total}=6^4=1296.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"152\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>We now work on the favorable cases.\n</p><p>Suppose the four numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/b/d8b8490a47ba3063da2731316f5d65dc5cf731ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be split as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7eae8643f68b95a0f2f7d2a6221ad3405790be24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[N=a+b=c+d.\\]\" width=\"147\" height=\"14\" />\nWe do casework on the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4a6d41204181432504f1108ded79e4a49e0e03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> Notice that a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> can be obtained in the same number of ways as a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/8/3c844ed79019bd39f4aa9720c6160a3ba50ed7b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14-n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> can be obtained. Thus:\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/4/df49ab19581b33197743316c6da3a6bc6568aaa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{n=2:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> A sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be obtained only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/8/3b852c261d9ee3e2134cde7ddd207035a4bbd110.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=b=c=d=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"148\" height=\"14\" /> Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> case.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c1d3f4b6abbaa668a9df423f2a4ac3f2826cdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{n=3:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> A sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be obtained as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/3/523e883c8edab64b14ad9358ba9d03203dedc209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3=1+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" /> thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/220e78f1fb76621bef824b0ce918b81339667b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!\\cdot 2!}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/7/a2707b75d629dcb3c49a3b84c72e7ba79d32d435.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{n=4:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> A sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be obtained as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd7e18cb9f71e92e1f5895eeddef3f10a5e04ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4=1+3=2+2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"17\" /> which produces the three possibilities of\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5c1ee2fed06e8b7371414f6fb5f3d3cff32d343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2,2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> case.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf3c848c95d84b66eed1413ddcac59b2509aa13a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1,3,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/0/220e78f1fb76621bef824b0ce918b81339667b58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!\\cdot 2!}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63bf5f80666ed15f95b2e7bdb8f1572f301bc7d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,2,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aaefb7180bdd76b6056ae5a48a7b7bbc26ad2f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!}=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69201928efc7a63a7cce168d26c77c50f07e4b9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6+12=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/2499727a00bbdf2968f64fea7ae6f7c37f086515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{n=5:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> A sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be obtained as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/c/5bc2cdb310fd2bc7094b6ba91abceaef7015c063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5=1+4=2+3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"17\" /> which produces the three possibilities of\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/a/26a4f8715ead7f6e2d346654aea7007808198a4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2,3,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132b83a853e83ccbdcc564f69359264d6d8cd5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!\\cdot2!}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d68f7163db91394fdd93736104b3c66da145d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1,4,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132b83a853e83ccbdcc564f69359264d6d8cd5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!\\cdot2!}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/6/d06a60c2aa2075c3025ac906bb3315b0c768994c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,3,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/1593463d6fb7eaeb3427e06c069fc425fb4f60d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04cf177151e3af7b6867afbcaa2e7bcdcb4b1213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+6+24=36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/2/5a2c12da17369c1fb1d4b4607bcfe344c2c0b560.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{n=6:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> A sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be obtained as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/a/58a6e38224ad029857a45452082b56ef855b026f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6=1+5=2+4=3+3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"210\" height=\"17\" /> which produces the six possibilities of\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299a3e6137dbe538718cc85fa388acc889f9bbc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,3,3,3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> case.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/5/9e5e9d6cc800d31f439ba43790942815387c867d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,3,3,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aaefb7180bdd76b6056ae5a48a7b7bbc26ad2f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!}=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/ddaf2a482f8e0972a6ad924f4056e25772b9a78a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,3,3,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/e/aaefb7180bdd76b6056ae5a48a7b7bbc26ad2f03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!}=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"62\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/a/a7ae21e8edae70dc0296eef08e00a127b21e8716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1,5,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132b83a853e83ccbdcc564f69359264d6d8cd5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!\\cdot2!}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/5454950261f856fe5eb501db4da280333048d15d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,4,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/1593463d6fb7eaeb3427e06c069fc425fb4f60d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b513f2e7c2ac460fe999494fa04a43b78a58a69c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2,4,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132b83a853e83ccbdcc564f69359264d6d8cd5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!\\cdot2!}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\nThus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/3496ff679bc4ea2163dbd9f1046ded7d1a88e857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6+12+12+6+24=61$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"237\" height=\"15\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/60093dfd0632504d5445b80a68960b6a8fea4f17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{n=7:}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> A sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be obtained as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/7944f0ea0d104a56a13dac20d60f472173b3d085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6=1+6=2+5=3+4,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"210\" height=\"17\" /> which produces the six possibilities of\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/6/ac6ee0dab3e7f5b2530032fa289baff8512f7a7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,1,6,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132b83a853e83ccbdcc564f69359264d6d8cd5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!\\cdot2!}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/a/b9a0d2591051ce77b818bc57fbedfaaa9e23ab9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,2,5,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/1593463d6fb7eaeb3427e06c069fc425fb4f60d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a51ac9f16f1d9e38d7ad99fc1cdb080f6cb348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,3,4,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/1593463d6fb7eaeb3427e06c069fc425fb4f60d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b428cc17dd513b1fbfa4b77335ffda71ca9dc74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2,5,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132b83a853e83ccbdcc564f69359264d6d8cd5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!\\cdot2!}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e90fd61bf330560d8a3e96fe8b4130a45d0962f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,3,4,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/1593463d6fb7eaeb3427e06c069fc425fb4f60d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4!=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/1/7e13f8fcdf31bda707f3173b9ca15e47885a743d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,4,5,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> which produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132b83a853e83ccbdcc564f69359264d6d8cd5db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4!}{2!\\cdot2!}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"81\" height=\"39\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/c/09c650fc24430918c283b251eef9725a7561ca36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+24+24+6+24+6=90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"237\" height=\"15\" /> cases.\n</p><p><br />\nThis means, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/503f00569310ce8a007da1f6dcfcd2b8054d03dd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{Favorable} = 90 +2\\left(1+6+19+36+61\\right)=336.\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>This means\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/e/feea1bd766f1fa64ecd7e7c3c885678031901bd3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{Probability}=\\frac{\\textbf{Favorable}}{\\textbf{Total}}=\\frac{336}{1296}=\\boxed{\\frac{7}{27}}.\\]\" width=\"327\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO\" title=\"2016 UMO\">2016 UMO </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems\" title=\"2016 UMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 UMO Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.utmath.org/home\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 UMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 UMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 UMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 UMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2016 UMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2016 UMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_UMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2016 UMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Utah_Math_Olympiad\" title=\"Utah Math Olympiad\"> All UMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017183504\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.